---

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — RepMaths"
  description="Privacy Policy for RepMaths fitness, strength, nutrition, and body composition calculators."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated: September 13, 2026</p>

<h2>Overview</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what
  information may be collected when you use the RepMaths website and
  how third-party services such as Google Analytics and Google AdSense
  may process information.
</p>

<h2>Calculator Data</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths calculators are designed to perform calculations directly
  in your web browser. Information entered into a calculator, such as
  body weight, repetitions, height, or measurements, is processed
  locally by the calculator and is not intentionally sent to or stored
  on RepMaths servers.
</p>

<p>
  However, third-party services used on the website, such as analytics
  or advertising services, may collect information about your visit
  independently of the calculator itself.
</p>

<h2>Google Analytics</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths may use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the
  website and to improve its performance, content, and user experience.
</p>

<p>
  Google Analytics may collect information such as usage and session
  data, approximate geographic information, browser and device
  information, and identifiers used to distinguish users or sessions.
  The information collected depends on how Google Analytics is
  configured on the website.
</p>

<p>
  RepMaths does not intentionally send personally identifiable
  information to Google Analytics through calculator inputs or other
  website functionality.
</p>

<p>
  For more information about how Google Analytics handles data, see
  Google's documentation on
  <a
    href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    safeguarding data
  </a>.
</p>

<h2>Google AdSense &amp; Advertising Cookies</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths may use Google AdSense to display advertisements. Google and
  its advertising partners may use cookies, web beacons, IP addresses,
  or similar technologies to serve, measure, and personalize
  advertising.
</p>

<p>
  Depending on applicable settings, consent, and regional requirements,
  advertising may be personalized based on a user's previous visits to
  this or other websites. Third-party vendors and advertising partners
  may also place or read cookies on your browser when ads are served.
</p>

<p>
  You can manage Google's personalized advertising settings through
  <a
    href="https://adssettings.google.com"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    Google Ads Settings
  </a>.
</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths itself may use only the cookies or browser storage necessary
  for website functionality, if applicable. Third-party services such
  as Google Analytics and Google AdSense may use their own cookies or
  similar technologies.
</p>

<p>
  You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings.
  Blocking certain cookies may affect the functionality of some
  websites or services.
</p>

<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths may use third-party services for analytics, advertising,
  hosting, security, or other website functionality. These services
  may process information according to their own privacy policies and
  terms.
</p>

<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

<p>
  RepMaths is not directed specifically at children. We do not
  knowingly collect personal information from children through the
  calculator tools.
</p>

<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

<p>
  This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect
  changes to the website, third-party services, legal requirements,
  or our privacy practices. The "Last updated" date at the top of
  this page indicates when the policy was most recently revised.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p>
  If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how RepMaths
  handles information, please visit our
  <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
</p>
 </article>

  <style>
    .legal-page {
      margin-top: 32px;
    }

    .legal-page h2 {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      margin-top: 32px;
    }

    .legal-page p {
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-page a {
      color: var(--accent);
    }
  </style>
  </Base>
